      "message": "[error] Line 145: 🔴 `SIPCall::~SIPCall()` acquires `callMutex_` and then calls `stopCallRecovery()`, which tries to lock `callMutex_` again. This is a self-deadlock on teardown and can stall call cleanup threads. Fix by introducing a `stopCallRecoveryLocked()` helper that assumes the mutex is already held (or call `stopCallRecovery()` before taking the mutex).",
      "revId": "3913b542e8c3dac983a59218925652a66c524236",
